    {
      "id": "15QxqCEqX7e25SMHanDA3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1781.2956592899488,
      "y": 4105.959862826325,
      "width": 2969.998779296875,
      "height": 2025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b17",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 489022962,
      "version": 1691,
      "versionNonce": 283411332,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789902112507,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Final Practice\n\nBookMyShow, GoogleDocs, TinyUrl, HashMap impl, SplitWise, Inventory Management, E-Commerce, ATM/Vending Machine, Snake and Ladder, \nParking Management, Elevator Management, Rate Limiter, Notification System(HLD) , Uber\n\n// Redis, Kafka(Internal Impl), Pub Sub, Indexing, Composite Index, Load Balancer, API Gateway, CDN, SQL/NoSQL, 0 to Million User, Google search works\n@Transactional, Java / Spring Boot, SOLID, Normalisation, Denormalisation, ACID/BASE, CAP\n\nindexing, sharding vs partition, kafka, redis pubsub vs kafka, zookeper, load balancer, sse / wss, cursor vs offset pagination\n\nsdlc, testing, deployment (red green/canary)\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLLD Revision\n\n1. BookMyShow\n\nFlow - \n1. User comes to website\n2. User will provide the location\n3. User can search for a movie\n4. User will select a particular theatre or date\n5. User will be able to see shows\n6. User will select seats in a show\n7. User will book it and do payment.\n8. Book the tickets\n\nEntities - \n1. Movie\n2. Theatre\n3. Show\n4. Seat\n5. Screen\n6. Ticket\n7. Booking\n8. Payment\n10. MovieManager\n11. TheatreManager\n12. BookMyShowApplication \n   \n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Final Practice\n\nBookMyShow, GoogleDocs, TinyUrl, HashMap impl, SplitWise, Inventory Management, E-Commerce, ATM/Vending Machine, Snake and Ladder, \nParking Management, Elevator Management, Rate Limiter, Notification System(HLD) , Uber\n\n// Redis, Kafka(Internal Impl), Pub Sub, Indexing, Composite Index, Load Balancer, API Gateway, CDN, SQL/NoSQL, 0 to Million User, Google search works\n@Transactional, Java / Spring Boot, SOLID, Normalisation, Denormalisation, ACID/BASE, CAP\n\nindexing, sharding vs partition, kafka, redis pubsub vs kafka, zookeper, load balancer, sse / wss, cursor vs offset pagination\n\nsdlc, testing, deployment (red green/canary)\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLLD Revision\n\n1. BookMyShow\n\nFlow - \n1. User comes to website\n2. User will provide the location\n3. User can search for a movie\n4. User will select a particular theatre or date\n5. User will be able to see shows\n6. User will select seats in a show\n7. User will book it and do payment.\n8. Book the tickets\n\nEntities - \n1. Movie\n2. Theatre\n3. Show\n4. Seat\n5. Screen\n6. Ticket\n7. Booking\n8. Payment\n10. MovieManager\n11. TheatreManager\n12. BookMyShowApplication \n   \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kLS2Cr3aa4ZLSwlhbkRac",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 3324.5728141173363,
      "y": 6274.864244065058,
      "width": 345.62767703519523,
